speechtext:
Yes. It reads:
(a)	If at the time the loss occurs the amount owing under the mortgage or hypothec for principal, interest, taxes, costs and other charges properly due on the mortgage account, is more than the amount advanced by the company two-thirds of the loss will be borne by His Majesty the King, represented as aforesaid, and one-third by the company;
(b)	If at the time the loss occurs the amount so owing under the mortgage or hypothec is less than the amount advanced by the company two-thirds of the loss will be borne by the company and one-third by His Majesty the King, represented as aforesaid.

The Bartman dam is
on East Berry creek in Alberta. There was storage for irrigation of approximately 700 acres of land in order to ensure a supply of winter feed. It was an earth dam with outlet pipe and spillway channel, estimated cost
S25,000.	Tenders were invited from the following :
E. O'Connor, Medicine Hat:
Poole Construction Co.. Ltd., Edmonton;
J. Millar, Western Construction Co., Edmonton ;
Special Municipal Areas Board, Edmonton;
W. B. Ramsay, Regina;
Gibbs Brothers, Lumsden, Saskatchewan;
Kearns & Mamoser, Shaunavon, Saskatchewan.
Tenders were received from the following only:
Special municipal areas board, $19,155.60;
Poole Construction Co., $19,332.50.
